<http://data.silknow.org/object/e9d8260d-1d7c-3521-b504-e15510cd2e5f/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The seated figure of a saint writing is possibly St. John the Evangelist.  Below him is the monogram I.H.S.  On each side are urns from which grow flowers on curving stems.  A raised cordonnet outlines part of the design.  The piece has been cut along the top and an edging of inferior workmanship added.  A similar piece illustrated in \"Antique Laces of American Collectors\" by Francis Morris and Marion Hague, plate 25, has in it the arms of the Pallavicini of Brannenburg"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e9d8260d-1d7c-3521-b504-e15510cd2e5f> .

<https://sws.geonames.org/3175395/>
